SUMMARY:Baobab
DESCRIPTION:The djembe drums dance and the ngoni’s strings sing as the griots tell a tale passed down from generation to generation. Long ago\, when the stars were still babies\, the trees and animals talked\, and a water-stealing sun burned overhead\, a baobab tree bore an unexpected and unusual gift. Featuring music from Mali and Senegal\, puppets large and small\, one naughty monkey\, and a witch with an itch to dance\, Baobab is a percussion-filled fable about a boy’s heroic quest to save his village from drought. At 6 pm in the lobby\, enjoy free children’s activities\, dancing from Imani Edu-tainers\, and small bites of African food from Upohar World Kitchen!
URL:https://visitlancastercity.com/event/baobab/
LOCATION:The Ware Center – Millersville University\, 42 N. Prince Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17603\, United States
CATEGORIES:Arts and Culture,First Friday
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://visitlancastercity.com/wp-content/uploads/Baobab_8521.jpg
END:VEVENT
